      "math_academy_id": "q-126790",
      "knowledge_point_id": "332fefd8-7de7-5a84-81e2-a2aa97be9b73",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Expected Value for a Random Variable with Uniform Probability",
      "problem": "A fair spinner has six sides labeled with the numbers $0,$ $1,$ $2,$ $3,$ $4,$ and $5.$ If the spinner is spun, what is the expected value of the outcome?",
      "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the outcome of the spinner. Then the support is $S=\\{0,1,2,3,4,5\\},$ and the corresponding probabilities are all $\\frac{1}{6}:$\n\n$$\nf(0)=f(1)=f(2)=f(3)=f(4)=f(5)=\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(5)+5\\cdot f(5) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{6})+1(\\frac{1}{6})+2(\\frac{1}{6})+3(\\frac{1}{6})+4(\\frac{1}{6})+5(\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{2}{6}+\\frac{3}{6}+\\frac{4}{6}+\\frac{5}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+1+2+3+4+5}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
